[?2004l[?2004hroot@06fe72e0-cd7f-40a2-9ded-2df9a9bdb577:/app# cat > churn/impute.py <<'EOF'
[?2004l[?2004h> """Gap filling for upstream readings that arrive with holes (analytics export outages, devices offline).
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> The original implementation performed a backward‑fill followed by a forward‑fill, which could
[?2004l[?2004h> inject future ``app_minutes_7d`` values into earlier predictions. The specification for the
[?2004l[?2004h> ``app_minutes_7d`` feature states that we may only use the most recent earlier reading.
[?2004l[?2004h> Therefore we replace the logic with a simple forward‑fill (``ffill``) after sorting by
[?2004l[?2004h> ``customer_id`` and ``as_of``.
[?2004l[?2004h> """
[?2004l[?2004h> 
[?2004l[?2004h> from __future__ import annotations
